      },
      "repo": "alpha-studios-demo/bioscanner",
      "featured": true,
      "origin": "studio",
      "founderName": "",
      "story": "Bioscanner began in a biology lab where students spent hours matching specimens to reference books. It identifies plants, insects and microscope samples from a single photo, shows how sure it is, and explains what it saw so a person can check the answer. The recognition models run on our own servers behind a FastAPI service, with an iPhone app, an Android app and a web version for the lab bench. It is in open beta while we gather more labelled images from classrooms and field trips.",
